course: dictionary
lesson: 1110
title: Bravery
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Bravery means being brave: doing something good or right even when it is dangerous, hard or scary. Bravery does not mean having no fear at all. Brave people often feel scared too, and they do the right thing anyway.
explain: Look at the context. «Won back by matchless valour, consummate strategy, and a proper handling of sticks.» Valour is another word for bravery. Swap in bravery and the sentence still makes sense: "won back by matchless bravery, consummate strategy, and a proper handling of sticks."
explain: Bravery can show up in small moments too, like standing up for a friend who is being picked on, or telling the truth when it is hard. «Doing dares to be liked often backfires» reminds us that a silly dare is not bravery. People remember the silly thing, not the bravery.
fact: Bravery is being brave: doing something good or right even when it is dangerous, hard or scary.
fact: «Valour» means bravery.
fact: Bravery is not having no fear; it is facing your fear and acting well anyway.
fact: Bravery can mean standing up for others or telling the truth.
fact: The lion is a symbol of courage and strength on many flags and coats of arms, and «King Richard I was called the Lionheart for his bravery.»
exercise: «Won back by matchless valour, consummate strategy, and a proper handling of sticks.» What does valour mean? | Being late | A kind of stick | *Bravery | Bad weather
exercise: Ella says bravery means never being scared. Is she right? | No, bravery is a word for games | Yes, but only for animals | *No, brave people can feel scared and still do the right thing | Yes, brave people never feel any fear
exercise: «Doing dares to be liked often backfires: people remember the silly thing, not the bravery.» What does this suggest? | Doing dares makes everyone like you | Bravery is always silly | Dares always make people brave | *A silly dare is not the same as real bravery
test:
«King Richard I was called the Lionheart for his bravery.» Why was he called the Lionheart? | *For his bravery | For his cooking | For his fast running | For his short temper
Priya told the teacher the truth, even though it was hard and she felt scared. What is this an example of? | *Bravery | Bossiness | Boredom | Hunger
exam:
In «a symbol of courage and strength», courage is closest in meaning to which word? | *Bravery | Hunger | Sleepiness | Laughter
